# Tinybones: "Whenever Tinybones deals combat damage to a player, you may cast target nonland permanent card from that
# player's graveyard, and mana of any type can be spent to cast that spell." Bot2 bolts its own Llanowar Elves on turn 2, so
# its graveyard holds a creature card and an instant. On turn 3 Tinybones hits Bot2: the Lightning Bolt is no legal target
# (not a permanent card), so the Elves are the only one and are chosen without a question. Bot1 casts them as the ability resolves, paying their {G} with black
# mana from its Mox Jet, and they enter under Bot1's control. Lightning Bolt stays in Bot2's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Tinybones, the Pickpocket
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tinybones, the Pickpocket.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Tinybones, the Pickpocket)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Tinybones, the Pickpocket; Llanowar Elves
